        <mxCell id="note-tls" value="Objective 4 and the proposal’s ethical section commit to HTTPS/SSL.
That is applied here, at nginx. Running the project locally for
marking uses plain HTTP on localhost, where there is no network
to intercept." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1010" y="130" width="350" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-docker" value="docker-compose.yml defines all of this as containers on one
network, plus phpMyAdmin and the optional Flask courier service.

Honest caveat: Docker is not installed on the development
machine, so the container stack is defined but has not been run
end to end. The tested way to run it is in docs/01-SETUP.md." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fef2f2;strokeColor=#b91c1c;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1010" y="250" width="350" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-relative" value="The browser calls a relative /api, never an absolute address —
which is exactly why the same build works from a phone." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
